    {
      "name": "Order System",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create an Order",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\r\n    \"menuItemId\": 4,\r\n    \"quantity\": 1,\r\n    \"forceOrder\": true,\r\n    \"tableId\": 3,\r\n    \"status\": \"active\"\r\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://localhost:8080/orders",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "localhost"
              ],
              "port": "8080",
              "path": [
                "orders"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates an order record.\n\nReturns a response object with \"data\" and \"warningMsg\"\n\nAfter placing an order, backend will auto subtract ingredients required for the menu item from the inventory.\n\nWhen the \"forceOrder\" flag is set to \"false\":\n\n- If there are not enough ingredients left in the inventory, the order WILL NOT be placed and will give a warning message about it.\n    \n- If there are enough ingredients, warningMsg will be null.\n    \n\nWhen the \"forceOrder\" flag is set to \"true\":\n\n- If there are not enough ingredients left in the inventory, the order WILL BE placed and will give a warning message about it.\n    \n- If there are enough ingredients, warningMsg will be null."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get all orders of tableID",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://localhost:8080/orders/2",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "localhost"
              ],
              "port": "8080",
              "path": [
                "orders",
                "2"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns all \"active\" orders for given TableID."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create a Bulk Order",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\r\n    \"orderList\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"menuItemId\": 4,\r\n            \"quantity\": 1,\r\n            \"forceOrder\": false,\r\n            \"tableId\": 2\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"menuItemId\": 2,\r\n            \"quantity\": 3,\r\n            \"forceOrder\": false,\r\n            \"tableId\": 2\r\n        }\r\n    ]\r\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://localhost:8080/orders/bulk",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "localhost"
              ],
              "port": "8080",
              "path": [
                "orders",
                "bulk"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Adds and/or updates Orders in bulk .\n\nYou can convert any data file into this JSON body by just setting value of \"orderList\" attribute to the data that is converted to JSON.\n\neg.\n\n{\n\n\"orderList\": \\[ \\]\n\n}\n\nReturns a response object with \"data\" and \"warningMsg\"\n\nEach item will be checked before placing. Hence if a certain menu item cannot be ordered due to lack of ingredients:\n\n- that specific order will be SKIPPED and will give a warningMsg about it if \"forceOrder\" = false.\n    \n- that specific order will be PLACED and will give a warningMsg about it of \"forceOrder\" = true."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update an Order",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\r\n    \"createdDate\": \"2026-07-25T10:08:00Z\",\r\n    \"forceOrder\": false,\r\n    \"id\": 6,\r\n    \"menuItemId\": 4,\r\n    \"orderPrice\": 70,\r\n    \"quantity\": 3,\r\n    \"status\": \"active\",\r\n    \"tableId\": 2\r\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://localhost:8080/orders",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "localhost"
              ],
              "port": "8080",
              "path": [
                "orders"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Updates an order record.\n\nNote that assuming the ingredients have already been used from the inventory, the ingredients will NOT be restored in Inventory Table.\n\nHence, the ingredients will be depleted again after updating the request."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Generate Bill for Table ID",
